{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:23685637 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:23685637 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"23685637","source":"MED","pmid":"23685637","doi":"10.1097/ccm.0b013e31828a2a85","title":"Milrinone therapy for enterovirus 71-induced pulmonary edema and/or neurogenic shock in children: a randomized controlled trial.","authorString":"Chi CY, Khanh TH, Thoa le PK, Tseng FC, Wang SM, Thinh le Q, Lin CC, Wu HC, Wang JR, Hung NT, Thuong TC, Chang CM, Su IJ, Liu CC.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Chi CY","firstName":"Chia-Yu","lastName":"Chi","initials":"CY","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"National Institute of Infectious Diseases and Vaccinology, National Health Research Institutes, Miaoli County, Taiwan."}]}},{"fullName":"Khanh TH","firstName":"Truong Huu","lastName":"Khanh","initials":"TH"},{"fullName":"Thoa le PK","firstName":"Le Phan Kim","lastName":"Thoa","initials":"le PK"},{"fullName":"Tseng FC","firstName":"Fan-Chen","lastName":"Tseng","initials":"FC"},{"fullName":"Wang SM","firstName":"Shih-Min","lastName":"Wang","initials":"SM"},{"fullName":"Thinh le Q","firstName":"Le Quoc","lastName":"Thinh","initials":"le Q"},{"fullName":"Lin CC","firstName":"Chia-Chun","lastName":"Lin","initials":"CC"},{"fullName":"Wu HC","firstName":"Han-Chieh","lastName":"Wu","initials":"HC","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2638-7883"}},{"fullName":"Wang JR","firstName":"Jen-Ren","lastName":"Wang","initials":"JR"},{"fullName":"Hung NT","firstName":"Nguyen Thanh","lastName":"Hung","initials":"NT"},{"fullName":"Thuong TC","firstName":"Tang Chi","lastName":"Thuong","initials":"TC"},{"fullName":"Chang CM","firstName":"Chung-Ming","lastName":"Chang","initials":"CM"},{"fullName":"Su IJ","firstName":"Ih-Jen","lastName":"Su","initials":"IJ"},{"fullName":"Liu CC","firstName":"Ching-Chuan","lastName":"Liu","initials":"CC"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4127-4046"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8223-696X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2638-7883"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7","volume":"41","journalIssueId":2049307,"dateOfPublication":"2013 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2013,"printPublicationDate":"2013-07-01","journal":{"title":"Critical care medicine","medlineAbbreviation":"Crit Care Med","essn":"1530-0293","issn":"0090-3493","isoabbreviation":"Crit Care Med","nlmid":"0355501"}},"pubYear":"2013","pageInfo":"1754-1760","abstractText":"<h4>Objective</h4>Enterovirus 71-induced brainstem encephalitis with pulmonary edema and/or neurogenic shock (stage 3B) is associated with rapid mortality in children. In a small pilot study, we found that milrinone reduced early mortality compared with historical controls. This prospective, randomized control trial was designed to provide more definitive evidence of the ability of milrinone to reduce the 1-week mortality of stage 3B enterovirus 71 infections.<h4>Design</h4>Prospective, unicenter, open-label, randomized, controlled study.<h4>Setting</h4>Inpatient ward of a large tertiary teaching hospital in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.<h4>Patients</h4>Children (≤ 18 yr old) admitted with proven enterovirus 71-induced pulmonary edema and/or neurogenic shock.<h4>Interventions</h4>Patients were randomly assigned to receive intravenous milrinone (0.5 μg/kg/min) (n = 22) or conventional management (n = 19). Both groups received dopamine or dobutamine and intravenous immunoglobulin.<h4>Measurements and main results</h4>The primary endpoint was 1-week mortality. The secondary endpoints included length of ventilator dependence and hospital stay and adverse events. The median age was 2 years with a predominance of boys in both groups. The 1-week mortality was significantly lower, 18.2% (4/22) in the milrinone compared with 57.9% (11/19) in the conventional management group (relative risk = 0.314 [95% CI, 0.12-0.83], p = 0.01). The median duration of ventilator-free days was longer in the milrinone treatment group (p = 0.01). There was no apparent neurologic sequela in the survivors in either group, and no drug-related adverse events were documented.<h4>Conclusions</h4>Milrinone significantly reduced the 1-week mortality of enterovirus 71-induced pulmonary edema and/or neurogenic shock without adverse effects. Further studies are needed to determine whether milrinone might be useful to prevent progression of earlier stages of brainstem encephalitis.","affiliation":"National Institute of Infectious Diseases and Vaccinology, National Health Research Institutes, Miaoli County, Taiwan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Enterovirus Infections","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"MO","qualifierName":"mortality","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"VI","qualifierName":"virology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pulmonary Edema","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"MO","qualifierName":"mortality","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"VI","qualifierName":"virology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Shock","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"MO","qualifierName":"mortality","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"VI","qualifierName":"virology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Milrinone","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation"